From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: attrr <110731994+attrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:26:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cs35l36: boost peak current from 1600 mA at 0x10

BSTCVRT_PEAK_CUR counts 50 mA steps from 1600 mA at 0x10, up to 4500 mA
at 0x4a, its default (as cs35l41's, and cs35l36's own register defaults,
have it). Without the 0x10 a peak of 3700 mA (flame's, as stock's)
gives 0x2a, 2900 mA.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/cs35l36.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l36.c b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l36.c
index ff6bba003d61..4c53b7ee538b 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l36.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l36.c
@@ -1453,7 +1453,8 @@ static int cs35l36_handle_of_data(struct i2c_client *i2c_client,
 			return -EINVAL;
 		}
 
-		pdata->bst_ipk = (val - 1600) / 50;
+		/* 0x10 is 1600 mA, as the register's default 0x4a is 4500 */
+		pdata->bst_ipk = (val - 1600) / 50 + 0x10;
 	} else {
 		dev_err(&i2c_client->dev,
 			"Unable to find required parameter 'cirrus,boost-peak-milliamp'");
